eight Penn State fraternity members are  due in court today in connection with  the death of a student pledge 19  year-old Timothy Piazza died in February  after a fall a grand jury report says  the fall came during a fraternity hazing  ritual involving heavy drinking he hurt  his head and ruptured his spleen  prosecutors say that the fraternity  members waited about 12 hours before  they called for an ambulance the members  are also accused of then trying to cover  up the incident  Jericka Duncan is outside the fraternity  house in State College Pennsylvania  Jericho good morning good morning those  18 members of the Beta Theta Pi are  facing charges ranging from hazing to  aggravated assault now the National  Organization the National fraternity  said it has disbanded the group and said  it does not tolerate alcohol abuse or  hazing it's a sentiment that is shared  by the university president how could a  group of people who have committed  themselves to each other let something  like that happen Penn State University  President Eric Barron describes the  grand jury report on the incident  surrounding the death of Timothy Piazza  as sickening according to the report  Piazza arrived at the frat house on  February 2nd there he and 13 other  pledges took part in the gauntlet a sort  of alcohol obstacle course where the  pledges consumed approximately four to  five alcoholic beverages varying from  beer wine and liquor all within a two  minute time span an hour later the  report says Piazza fell down a flight of  stairs surveillance video inside the  frat house apparently shows him carried  up by four bethe brothers his body  appears limp his eyes closed and his  demeanor unconscious Piazza Falls  several more times throughout the night  hitting his head in some instances while  on the floor frat brothers step over his  body by 10 a.m. the next morning to fret  brothers found Piazza on the basement  floor they say he was cold to the touch  and his skin appeared pale but no one  called 911 until 42 minutes later  there's a friend who's unconscious  neither nerve uses coal Cheviot starting  that noise okay how old is he fears  right thing yes I guess arching years  old  the next day Tim Piazza was dead his  father called this a preventable and  senseless tragedy again it's did not  have to happen no parent should have to  deal with this  a grand jury determined Piazza died as a  direct result of extremely reckless  conduct of members of the beta  fraternity the report also says the  investigation shows an active attempt to  conceal and or destroy evidence by some  frat members Tom Klein represents the  Piazza family the lack of humanity the  lack of caring the lack of dignity of  the young men who did so much harm here  is unthinkable and it doesn't end with  just the criminal case since the release  of that grand jury report the university  has now launched its own investigation  and the university president tells me it  could very well lead to expulsion  Charlie Jericka thanks
 

